    "status": "present",
    "value": "A rectangular grid marks infected cells with 1 and healthy cells with 0. Each day you may build walls around exactly one connected infected region (4-directionally connected): choose the region that would infect the most healthy cells the next night. Building costs one wall per shared side between that region and a healthy neighbour. After that, every other region spreads to all healthy cells adjacent to it. Repeat until no region can spread further, or the whole grid is infected. Return the total number of walls built."
  },
